[{:db/id "q-41702/selection/663d76b089c95fe011ee6f811da647a542efd3bfbe7f64b930ce6b92ea236f59" :answer/id #uuid "7e3d2aa9-14a4-5abb-902d-864dcae498d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{0}dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702/selection/0955e5aa3e51020b84814c78dd1661b82ac3d21434bf6539e9c73b5e5d78f7e0" :answer/id #uuid "131e615e-2024-5d2b-a273-6d3d5bc51e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}(x+y)dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702/selection/578d3a826e4526b7d1d7b5c702a89e386899c30dedb8dc2b05308ad55e311bda" :answer/id #uuid "fe946125-1f14-584b-ade9-b15b89beb174" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{0}x\\,dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702/selection/426853ba176a7bb473fb3b1d9c11d3ceff0671528242a786b654a4c2704fceea" :answer/id #uuid "82cf829d-8d2d-5e41-9c68-aa70edee2614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{0}(x-y)dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702/selection/11ca19bcd2ea6ca87578ba95cc13379d3a94a8d3166bd493c8abcf4e8f5e1ed2" :answer/id #uuid "9065e90b-28dc-5ea8-aa7a-3068c329885f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{0}dy\\,dx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c949508-1128-595b-ad1a-a5a399d5a0db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-41702/selection/663d76b089c95fe011ee6f811da647a542efd3bfbe7f64b930ce6b92ea236f59" :answer-field/choices ["q-41702/selection/663d76b089c95fe011ee6f811da647a542efd3bfbe7f64b930ce6b92ea236f59" "q-41702/selection/0955e5aa3e51020b84814c78dd1661b82ac3d21434bf6539e9c73b5e5d78f7e0" "q-41702/selection/578d3a826e4526b7d1d7b5c702a89e386899c30dedb8dc2b05308ad55e311bda" "q-41702/selection/426853ba176a7bb473fb3b1d9c11d3ceff0671528242a786b654a4c2704fceea" "q-41702/selection/11ca19bcd2ea6ca87578ba95cc13379d3a94a8d3166bd493c8abcf4e8f5e1ed2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-41702" :question/id #uuid "43097466-6b45-5435-93fb-440587805a9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-41702" :question/problem "Consider the closed curve $C,$ which is the boundary of the region enclosed by $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis, for $\\pi \\le x\\le 2\\pi .$ Express ${\\int }_{C}xdx-(x-y)dy$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066044/assets/264cb888010525848f647669653d34383535dd32e6ac264927105540c3b85f9f.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=-(x-y).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):\\pi \\le x\\le 2\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le y\\le 0}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the Green's Theorem we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}xdx-(x-y)dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{0}dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-41702/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-41702"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection/c616911ec86eadc0dbfa82fad6582dcf4954c62d4464facc7fdfee85d871546f" :answer/id #uuid "4fbc58e1-7638-53ef-96ef-0fafc474c5fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection/4a1efcc36c468ba07c42ea9a10b949251b5764432c649334fa6fb06211e88eb4" :answer/id #uuid "9c386041-9e1c-58c3-8b3e-f5b308070b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection/7cd03b578ee86fef48cb515e5cddef90cb0d1be25221816bccdfe355374ad6cf" :answer/id #uuid "2f714b0e-a5cc-54fb-b099-b1ad69ac4e04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection/dd39294b8249de2631091885501403ab3ef6a170f7b242f3ef770d519dd749bd" :answer/id #uuid "8d74c7c2-955b-58c1-9754-9f01792a9be6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection/dcbd5c76c450e77c9d9b0e9229fd63843c24dda181f4bc1ee3ddc11077d51028" :answer/id #uuid "73a3bf70-1ff5-56a2-be1b-298dfbcfc8a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99195091-e352-5269-9cd2-10d1dde94606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109130/selection/7cd03b578ee86fef48cb515e5cddef90cb0d1be25221816bccdfe355374ad6cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-109130/selection/c616911ec86eadc0dbfa82fad6582dcf4954c62d4464facc7fdfee85d871546f" "q-109130/selection/4a1efcc36c468ba07c42ea9a10b949251b5764432c649334fa6fb06211e88eb4" "q-109130/selection/7cd03b578ee86fef48cb515e5cddef90cb0d1be25221816bccdfe355374ad6cf" "q-109130/selection/dd39294b8249de2631091885501403ab3ef6a170f7b242f3ef770d519dd749bd" "q-109130/selection/dcbd5c76c450e77c9d9b0e9229fd63843c24dda181f4bc1ee3ddc11077d51028"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109130" :question/id #uuid "6a0fcc5b-0558-5150-a8c6-d2887d157c75" :question/math-academy-id "q-109130" :question/problem "Consider the triangle $C$ in the plane with vertices $(0,2),(1,0)$ and $(2,0),$ and the region $D$ bounded by $C.$ According to Green's theorem, \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dy={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nCalculate the function $f(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066044/assets/8e3efc3f9c58fb0f9a84144e97a300b6ab2a4011d47ee0d2bae1edc8a3f721cd.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})\\,dx+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-109130/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf385144-2f48-5874-8c0d-dec31d8fc6e3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "78f09a34-4196-581e-977b-e5b599f3b562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "d3aae30a-5e41-5474-8a31-6d148951bc69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "5d0ac646-c124-5e6f-a171-a0ed5363dc84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "62bae293-97dd-5fcf-a6b8-aded44d3a2bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "addb2e9b-c846-554e-9300-422f5f8be413" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee53ccd9-f545-57f5-b44a-a9c3587fd91e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109151/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-109151/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-109151/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-109151/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-109151/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-109151/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109151" :question/id #uuid "f4dd77af-0cc1-5c9d-aba4-c3fd1a97e97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109151" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$ where $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}-{y}^{2},{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}⟩$ and $C$ is the boundary of the square with vertices at $(-1,-1),$ $(1,-1),$ $(1,1)$ and $(-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066044/assets/574172dda3031b9bb44dbcfb46265453ae543a75bccf8db24e93625e7154bba9.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-{y}^{2})\\,dx+({e}^{y}+{x}^{2})\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{x}-{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{y}+{x}^{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{x}-{y}^{2})\\,dx+({e}^{y}+{x}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x+2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(2x+2y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[2xy+{y}^{2}]}_{-1}^{1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(2x(1)+(1)^{2}-2x(-1)-(-1)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}4x\\,dx \\\\  & =2{[{x}^{2}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2[(1)^{2}-(-1)^{2}] \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109151/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" :answer/id #uuid "ec24f900-45a6-57e4-a4b1-a68b3b11e556" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection/266f8fc061957f6a8756e2983e0b79d344c2a4f70b57783044e99932e211632d" :answer/id #uuid "53b50e0b-1685-5511-adcf-6cb080ed03b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{27}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection/7b946525452c2bd905f5e1c9d8392a8b8e021cf34430f6888d8a5408c38e8e12" :answer/id #uuid "acede4b9-07ea-5c6b-aaf1-8f003b260d50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{64}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection/954787884460f2d3ed41cc92383c999ac9e65bfa543536baab5a88bba82242a2" :answer/id #uuid "c776220c-b6ec-5360-88c8-9547ac477cd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{27}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection/144b57e26ff6ca7ce113619b5774049a59a763e33c4a946917e21d1cc7a45977" :answer/id #uuid "2d1a0da9-b07b-5a63-9844-68f1b729f0d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{81}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "17fe58b7-a2f7-5e1e-a35c-276d06a5ea08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109166/selection/144b57e26ff6ca7ce113619b5774049a59a763e33c4a946917e21d1cc7a45977" :answer-field/choices ["q-109166/selection/1114f773249b584f03ae90d8348b5b14abd566a3f244c0aad51e974a9460892e" "q-109166/selection/266f8fc061957f6a8756e2983e0b79d344c2a4f70b57783044e99932e211632d" "q-109166/selection/7b946525452c2bd905f5e1c9d8392a8b8e021cf34430f6888d8a5408c38e8e12" "q-109166/selection/954787884460f2d3ed41cc92383c999ac9e65bfa543536baab5a88bba82242a2" "q-109166/selection/144b57e26ff6ca7ce113619b5774049a59a763e33c4a946917e21d1cc7a45977"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109166" :question/id #uuid "d92cf6d2-0783-508f-af3a-287ef5da8ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-109166" :question/problem "Use Green's theorem to evaluate ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr,$ where $F(x,y)=⟨2x+{y}^{2},{x}^{2}+2y⟩$ and $C$ is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}$ and the lines $y=0$ and $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066044/assets/fafd281fc63fb276c9759fd84f722096d494aa3e3fe9441f43aa6ecd1f9dfda9.png)\n\nFirst, notice that we can rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∮}_{C}(2x+{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy\n$$\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+2y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}(2x+{y}^{2})\\,dx+({x}^{2}+2y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2x-2y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}/3}(2x-2y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2xy-{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{{x}^{2}/3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{9})dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{45}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)^{4}}{6}-\\frac{(3)^{5}}{45} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}-\\frac{27}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109166/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11d3f9e1-dad0-51d4-86a9-e0c49465cc3c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection/e47a67ce9783f68b4791ffe8d648e5decb7c53fc12bd0708cdd3f91a8883c474" :answer/id #uuid "3ff8cdb0-23f3-50d0-9d7e-d0fee963e7cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{3y-{y}^{2}}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection/71e351433271ae2a985af433d253e0de4aa1f38a67de2e0ac1023acbe0dddb18" :answer/id #uuid "6fb682f6-f8de-52e4-9d26-c76db4d788f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{4y-{y}^{2}}({e}^{y}-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection/a7fd554056955a972103b462ebe580bfca9c96cbca124bd929151bf8b3a895d7" :answer/id #uuid "47bcc0ab-20d8-5546-a834-0f22aa069a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{4y-{y}^{2}}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection/c526c44d4b5e9ac23170850be2389623b67d4952f5f02c95cdce912188d538b5" :answer/id #uuid "3f684af2-7293-5eb0-8f7c-7ae32d212c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{4y-{y}^{2}}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection/c92e7501f831231435e16a559effeac21f7f88030b556b008bd0c1bf85645e67" :answer/id #uuid "5127880c-4426-5aaf-a60b-397ebad58a22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{4y-{y}^{2}}(2x{e}^{y}-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c819e7d3-8e3d-5242-a37b-f5103a40944f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-109249/selection/a7fd554056955a972103b462ebe580bfca9c96cbca124bd929151bf8b3a895d7" :answer-field/choices ["q-109249/selection/e47a67ce9783f68b4791ffe8d648e5decb7c53fc12bd0708cdd3f91a8883c474" "q-109249/selection/71e351433271ae2a985af433d253e0de4aa1f38a67de2e0ac1023acbe0dddb18" "q-109249/selection/a7fd554056955a972103b462ebe580bfca9c96cbca124bd929151bf8b3a895d7" "q-109249/selection/c526c44d4b5e9ac23170850be2389623b67d4952f5f02c95cdce912188d538b5" "q-109249/selection/c92e7501f831231435e16a559effeac21f7f88030b556b008bd0c1bf85645e67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-109249" :question/id #uuid "6909bb91-13a3-5626-9d74-7589d0e445fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-109249" :question/problem "Consider the closed curve $C,$ which is the boundary of the region enclosed by the curves $x=y$ and $x=4y-{y}^{2}.$ Express ${∮}_{C}({e}^{y}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,dx+(2x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,dy$ as a repeated integral." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D$, then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ and the curve $C$ for this case are shown below.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066044/assets/239867aec8cff7840667d2f4eafa9bc97d4fc5af09b684d863fef06fd8fd28ad.png)\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={e}^{y}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=2x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2{e}^{y}+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can express the region $D$ as a type II region as follows:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):y\\le x\\le 4y-{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's Theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}({e}^{y}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,dx+(2x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2{e}^{y}+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-{e}^{y}-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{4y-{y}^{2}}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-109249/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48652211-e469-55b9-96cb-2526a4135d34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-109249"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
